WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.597
Real data is messy, so functions often need a safe way to handle predictable problems.

00:00:06.597 --> 00:00:10.592
Safe_integer tries to convert text to an integer.

00:00:10.592 --> 00:00:16.497
The string “42” converts successfully and returns forty-two.

00:00:16.497 --> 00:00:24.024
The text “forty-two” raises a ValueError, so the except block catches it and returns None instead.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:29.968
Try values such as “007”, “3.5”, and an empty string.

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:37.503
Notice that not every string that looks numeric in some way is a valid integer.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:41.028
This is a simple example of defensive programming.
